# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# Generated data (raw/ is tracked; these are rebuilt from it)
data/processed/*
data/final/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/final/.gitkeep

# Model artefacts
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.h5

# Outputs
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXCEPTIONS: these are NOT regenerable outputs, they are EVIDENCE.
#
# The rule above is right for anything rebuilt from data/raw. It is wrong for
# the artefacts later instruments ANCHOR against, because "frozen" was being
# enforced by nothing but a file timestamp and good intentions. Instrument 5's
# C1 equivalence check reads phase3_reg_surface.csv; Instrument 4's R7 reads
# phase3_ablation_fold_summary.csv. Either could have been silently
# regenerated with no diff to detect it.
#
# A pre-declaration in particular exists to be unamendable after the fact, and
# an unversioned pre-declaration cannot do that job at all.
#
# FROZEN_MANIFEST.txt records the SHA-256 of every file listed here, so
# tampering is detectable independently of git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# pre-declarations - the whole point is that they cannot move
!outputs/phase4_dynamic_state_predeclaration.txt

# the frozen evaluation contract
!outputs/phase0_evaluation_folds.csv
!outputs/phase0_evaluation_spec.csv
!outputs/phase0_evaluation_spec.json

# Phase 2 reference values carried forward into Phase 4
!outputs/phase2_base_rate_fold_summary.csv
!outputs/phase2_elo_fold_summary.csv
# Elo v1's per-match probabilities, which its RPS is derived from. FROZEN
# MANIFEST LISTED IT AND GIT NEVER CARRIED IT - a clone on 2026-09-03 reported
# it MISSING while the manifest called it frozen. A frozen artefact that
# exists on one laptop only is not frozen, it is local.
!outputs/phase2_elo_metrics_full.csv
!outputs/phase2_poisson_dc_fold_summary.csv

# Phase 3: THE FEATURE FILE every rung is built from, and the inventory that
# independently describes it. Both were untracked until Phase 4's DS7 went
# live at D3 and could not assert "byte-identical to the frozen Phase 3
# artefacts" against an artefact that was not frozen. The largest hole this
# block has had: D0-D4, the ablation, the ceiling and the regularisation
# surface every one of them read phase3_features.csv.
!outputs/phase3_features.csv
!outputs/phase3_feature_inventory.csv

# Phase 3: the lambda = 1 reference (R7), Instruments 4 and 5, and the freeze
!outputs/phase3_ablation_fold_summary.csv
!outputs/phase3_ablation_ladder.csv
!outputs/phase3_reg_*.csv
!outputs/phase3_ceiling_*.csv
!outputs/phase3_frozen_regularisation.json

# Phase 4 tier-2 resolution - the evidence that decides what D2 is built from
!outputs/phase4_tier2_*.csv

# Phase 4 DC passthrough - the diagnostic that decided the link is sound, and
# the point-in-time state it wrote. The ladder's S1 ANCHORS against
# phase4_dc_state.csv, so leaving it unversioned was the exact half-protection
# this exception block exists to prevent.
!outputs/phase4_dc_state.csv
!outputs/phase4_passthrough_*.csv

# Phase 4 ladder - D0, D1, D2, their audit trail and the state they are built
# from. The rescaled rung of Amendment 4 writes to its own filenames, so these
# stay the artefacts the first run produced.
!outputs/phase4_dynamic_state.csv
!outputs/phase4_ladder_*.csv

# The D3/D4 instrument's crash-safety copy. Deliberately NOT under outputs/,
# so that DS10's frozen_manifest.py --verify cannot see a half-finished run's
# tables as unlisted frozen artefacts. Never evidence; deleted freely.
.d34_inprogress/

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Phase 4 Amendments 4 and 5 - the rescaled rung and D2-static
!outputs/phase4_a4_*.csv
!outputs/phase4_static_state.csv

# Phase 4 D3 and D4 - Block C and Block X on top of D2 rescaled, and the
# expected_total_goals redundancy diagnostic that preceded them.
!outputs/phase4_d34_*.csv
!outputs/phase4_etg_*.csv

# Phase 5 Instrument B - the market benchmark and the calibration audit.
# The odds source itself is small, immutable and the thing the benchmark
# stands on, so it is tracked rather than re-downloaded: a re-download that
# moves a hash is a NEW SOURCE, not a refresh.
!outputs/phase5_*.csv

# Phase 5 E1 - SoT ratings and the rolling shot-residual block.
!outputs/phase5_e1a_*.csv
!outputs/phase5_e1b_*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE UNDERSTAT SEASON TABLES, WHICH ARE THE WRONG ARTEFACT FOR THE xG ARM
#
# data/league-chemp*.csv are season-aggregate league tables - 20 team rows of
# totals, four distinct files for five seasons, two of them byte-identical,
# 2024-25 absent. A SEASON TOTAL CONTAINS THE MATCHES BEING PREDICTED, so they
# cannot serve the arm at any resolution. PHASE5_XG_PREDECLARATION.txt needs
# MATCH-LEVEL xG.
#
# Ignored rather than merely untracked, so that a `git add -A` cannot sweep
# them into the repo and make them look like an accepted source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/league-chemp*.csv

# Phase 6 - the holdout freeze. The validation artefact is EVIDENCE of the
# sign-off, not a regenerable output: it records which constants were checked
# against which freeze text on which day. Versioned for the same reason the
# pre-declarations are.
!outputs/phase6_freeze_validation.csv
!outputs/phase6_*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SOURCE WATCH'S SNAPSHOTS.
#
# scripts/phase6_source_watch.py fetches the live 2026-27 E0 file monthly to
# check its SHAPE. Those snapshots are diagnostic, not evidence: they change
# every month, they are mid-season, and no scoring code reads them. Keeping
# them out of git is also what keeps the live season's scorelines out of the
# repository until the holdout is deliberately acquired at season end.
#
# The real E0_2627.csv arrives in data/raw/Odds/ once, in May 2027, as a
# separate act - and a re-download that moves a hash is a NEW SOURCE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/watch/

# The watch's own dated audit trail is evidence, and is covered by the
# outputs/phase6_*.csv exception above.
